From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/27] prime: take LZT1 attestations over DATUM (0x5A) and
 verify them on the first share

SOV-P-002 W7. A gateway sends job_id | variant | A | sig | 0xFE ahead of
its first share on a job; primed keeps it per job x coinbase variant and
decides it once, when the first share on that coinbase arrives, with
authorship::verify against the job and the session's identity key as G.
A verified attestation from a registered, non-house key joins the
attested-job set as the HTTP ingest's does. Every verdict is counted in
/sovereignty.json (attest{received,verified,failed,reasons,last}) and
appended to sovereignty-attest.jsonl, rotated daily. Nothing happens with
sovereignty-mode off; older Primes ignore the sub-command.

wire/examples/lzt1_check checks a 0x5A message against its coinbase for
other gateway implementations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
